{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ssa_templates",
    "description": "Expression-template library for the PISM shallow-shelf-approximation (SSA) stress-balance component (stage 2 of the eqice project): the flow-line membrane-divergence discretization, the face stiffness (4*nuH at a staggered face, nu from the face strain rate), and the surface-gradient rule with the SSAFD wall treatment. This file declares the flow-line geometry contract itself (metaparameter N = cell count, index sets x and face) rather than importing the cartesian_uniform_1d grid library, because the PISM SSAFD stencil evaluates the flux coefficient at the FACE from face quantities (strain rate, thickness) instead of averaging cell values -- see the rule description for the mapping to SSAFDBase.cc. Free names in template bodies (constants and parameters such as H, B, n, gamma_0, epsilon, dx, delta_p, ...) resolve against the importing model's declared parameters (esm-spec 9.6.1); templates referencing other templates (effective_viscosity) require the importing model to also import ./ice_rheology_templates.esm. Reference implementation: PISM v2.3.2 (stage1/pism/src/stressbalance/ssa/SSAFDBase.cc, SSAFD.cc)."
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "N": { "type": "integer", "default": 60, "description": "Number of cells along x (the flow-line SSA grid; the PISM run has Mx=61 cells of which the last is ice-free ocean, so the shelf itself occupies 60 cells)." }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "x": { "kind": "interval", "size": "N" },
    "face": { "kind": "interval", "size": "N" }
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "ssa_face_stiffness": {
      "description": "SSAFD face stiffness kf = 4*(nu*H_face + epsilon) at the face between two adjacent cells with velocities u_i, u_j and thicknesses H_i, H_j: nu = effective_viscosity(B, gamma_0 + u_x^2, n) with u_x = (u_j - u_i)/dx the face strain rate and gamma_0 the Schoof regularization (flow_law.Schoof_regularizing_velocity/length squared), H_face = (H_i + H_j)/2, and epsilon = stress_balance.ssa.epsilon the nuH regularization added to keep nuH bounded away from zero (SSAFDBase::compute_nuH_cfbc: nu*H + nuH_regularization; the factor 4 is the shallow-shelf x-momentum coefficient 4*nuH*u_x, see the divergence rule). The effective viscosity itself (0.5*B*(eps+gamma)^((1-n)/(2n))) is imported by reference from ice_rheology_templates.esm, so the importing model must import that library too (same contract as sia_templates.esm).",
      "params": ["u_i", "u_j", "H_i", "H_j"],
      "match": { "op": "ssa_face_stiffness", "args": ["u_i", "u_j", "H_i", "H_j"] },
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          4.0,
          {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "effective_viscosity",
                    "args": [
                      "B",
                      {
                        "op": "^",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "/",
                            "args": [
                              { "op": "-", "args": ["u_j", "u_i"] },
                              "dx"
                            ]
                          },
                          2.0
                        ]
                      },
                      "gamma_0",
                      "n"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      0.5,
                      { "op": "+", "args": ["H_i", "H_j"] }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "epsilon"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "ssa_surface_gradient_x": {
      "description": "x-component of the surface gradient with the SSAFD wall treatment (SSAFDBase::compute_driving_stress): centered difference (h[i+1] - h[i-1])/(2*dx) in the interior; at the domain edges the surface is extrapolated with zero gradient (the ghost value equals the boundary cell), giving the one-sided differences (h[2] - h[1])/(2*dx) at i=1 and (h[N] - h[N-1])/(2*dx) at i=N. The i=N rule is exactly PISM's treatment at the calving front: floating ice next to ice-free ocean uses the one-sided difference divided by 2 (constant extrapolation of the surface beyond the front). Verified against the dumped driving stress: -rho*g*H*h_x reproduces the dump column taud_x to double precision at every cell.",
      "params": ["h"],
      "match": { "op": "ssa_surface_gradient_x", "args": ["h"] },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [[2, { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }]],
          [[1, 1]],
          [["N", "N"]]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": ["i"],
            "args": ["h"],
            "ranges": { "i": [2, { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }] },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["h", { "op": "+", "args": ["i", 1] }] },
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["h", { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 1] }] }
                  ]
                },
                { "op": "*", "args": [2.0, "dx"] }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  { "op": "index", "args": ["h", 2] },
                  { "op": "index", "args": ["h", 1] }
                ]
              },
              { "op": "*", "args": [2.0, "dx"] }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  { "op": "index", "args": ["h", "N"] },
                  { "op": "index", "args": ["h", { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }] }
                ]
              },
              { "op": "*", "args": [2.0, "dx"] }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "ssa_flowline_membrane_divergence": {
      "description": "Conservative-flow-line SSA membrane divergence div(4*nu*H*grad u) with the SSAFD (PISM) face evaluation and boundary rows, matching D(k*D(u,x),x) at priority 10 so it fires on the whole compound before any plain-D rule could lower the inner derivative (esm-spec 9.6.3). Match-scoped with where {u:{shape:[x]}, k:{shape:[x]}} so it fires only on this grid's x-shaped fields; `k` is the operator-form coefficient the consumer declares (the varcoeff-family contract), but the body does NOT read it: PISM's SSAFD evaluates the flux coefficient at each FACE from face quantities -- the face strain rate (u_j - u_i)/dx and the mean thickness (H_i + H_j)/2 -- via compute_nuH_cfbc, which is not the arithmetic mean of cell-centered coefficients. The body computes kf = 4*(nu*H_face + epsilon) at the faces through the ssa_face_stiffness template (free names H, B, n, gamma_0, epsilon, dx resolve in the consuming model). Regions (makearray, later regions overwrite earlier): interior [2, N-1] the SSAFD flux difference (kf[i+1/2]*(u[i+1]-u[i]) - kf[i-1/2]*(u[i]-u[i-1]))/dx^2, matching the PISM matrix row eq1 (SSAFDBase::assemble_matrix: off-diagonals -4*c.w/dx^2 and -4*c.e/dx^2 with c = nuH at the faces; the y-couplings vanish for the flow-line state, which is uniform in y, and the v-equation decouples); [1,1] the divergence at the Dirichlet cell with the left-wall flux set to 0 (finite placeholder; the dynamics replace this row by the prescribed-velocity penalty, see the consuming model); [N,N] the calving-front row: the east-face flux is PRESCRIBED as the front pressure difference delta_p (SSAFDBase::assemble_rhs: result.u = taud.u + (E-W)*delta_p/dx with E=1 at the ice-free-ocean face and the matrix E-weight dropped), i.e. fluxdiv[N] = (delta_p - kf[N-1/2]*(u[N]-u[N-1])/dx)/dx. `delta_p` is a free name supplied by the consumer (the front pressure difference H*(0.5*rho_i*g*H - P_water)). The steady equation the divergence enters is div(flux) = rho*g*H*h_x (SSAFD solves L*u = taud with L = -div and taud = -rho*g*H*h_x), so the residual of the membrane balance is fluxdiv - rho*g*H*h_x.",
      "params": ["u", "k"],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "k",
              { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "x" }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
      },
      "where": { "u": { "shape": ["x"] }, "k": { "shape": ["x"] } },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [[2, { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }]],
          [[1, 1]],
          [["N", "N"]]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": ["i"],
            "args": ["u"],
            "ranges": { "i": [2, { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }] },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "ssa_face_stiffness",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", "i"] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", { "op": "+", "args": ["i", 1] }] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["H", "i"] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["H", { "op": "+", "args": ["i", 1] }] }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", { "op": "+", "args": ["i", 1] }] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", "i"] }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "ssa_face_stiffness",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 1] }] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", "i"] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["H", { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 1] }] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["H", "i"] }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", "i"] },
                            { "op": "index", "args": ["u", { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 1] }] }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                { "op": "*", "args": ["dx", "dx"] }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "ssa_face_stiffness",
                    "args": [
                      { "op": "index", "args": ["u", 1] },
                      { "op": "index", "args": ["u", 2] },
                      { "op": "index", "args": ["H", 1] },
                      { "op": "index", "args": ["H", 2] }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      { "op": "index", "args": ["u", 2] },
                      { "op": "index", "args": ["u", 1] }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              { "op": "*", "args": ["dx", "dx"] }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "delta_p",
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "ssa_face_stiffness",
                            "args": [
                              { "op": "index", "args": ["u", { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }] },
                              { "op": "index", "args": ["u", "N"] },
                              { "op": "index", "args": ["H", { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }] },
                              { "op": "index", "args": ["H", "N"] }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": "-",
                            "args": [
                              { "op": "index", "args": ["u", "N"] },
                              { "op": "index", "args": ["u", { "op": "-", "args": ["N", 1] }] }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      "dx"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "dx"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
